00:14:08.189 --> 00:14:11.319
but, you know, she's tired, so-

230
00:14:13.965 --> 00:14:17.368
Naomi, can you
open your mouth for me
and, um, tilt your head back?

231
00:14:17.438 --> 00:14:19.805
This is gonna be
a little uncomfortable.

232
00:14:25.618 --> 00:14:29.556
[Coughs]
Yeah. There's swelling,
indenting the esophagus.

233
00:14:29.625 --> 00:14:31.184
Is that why she choked?

234
00:14:31.261 --> 00:14:34.892
- We'll need to do an X-ray.
- What? No. The baby.
You said no X-rays.

235
00:14:34.968 --> 00:14:36.527
It's important.

236
00:14:36.604 --> 00:14:39.073
She has a three-centimeter mass...

237
00:14:39.142 --> 00:14:41.077
in her right upper lobe.

238
00:14:41.145 --> 00:14:45.517
Maybe it's a granuloma.
No. There's no calcification.

239
00:14:51.897 --> 00:14:55.232
It's small-cell lung cancer.

240
00:14:55.302 --> 00:14:58.136
The tumor's starting to press
against your esophagus.

241
00:14:58.207 --> 00:15:02.772
It hasn't metastasized,
but it has spread to other parts
of your lung, so we can't operate.

242
00:15:02.848 --> 00:15:05.215
Wait. That doesn't make sense.

243
00:15:05.286 --> 00:15:07.983
She had, uh, kidney failure
and brain problems.

244
00:15:08.057 --> 00:15:12.724
Some cancer patients
get what are called
paraneoplastic syndromes.

245
00:15:12.798 --> 00:15:15.563
You were making antibodies
to fight the tumor.

246
00:15:15.636 --> 00:15:17.764
They got sidetracked
and attacked other cells.

247
00:15:17.840 --> 00:15:21.471
Your brain first.
Then your liver, kidneys.

248
00:15:21.546 --> 00:15:23.879
Even the nerves
that control your eyelids.

249
00:15:23.951 --> 00:15:27.821
That's called Lambert-Eaton syndrome.
It told us the tumor was in the lungs.

250
00:15:30.027 --> 00:15:32.394
How bad is it?

251
00:15:34.768 --> 00:15:38.171
Small-cell is the most aggressive
kind of lung cancer.

252
00:15:38.242 --> 00:15:42.909
The five-year survival rate
is only about 10% to 15%.

253
00:15:44.252 --> 00:15:47.587
Which is why we have to start you
on chemo and radiation right away.

254
00:15:47.657 --> 00:15:51.322
- Radiation? What about the baby?
- You'll need a C-section
before you can start the treatment.

255
00:15:51.397 --> 00:15:53.866
I can get you in
first thing tomorrow morning.

256
00:15:53.934 --> 00:15:56.199
What are the chances
my baby will survive?

257
00:15:56.272 --> 00:16:00.370
Pretty good.
Twenty-eight weeks, so about 80%.

258
00:16:02.182 --> 00:16:04.174
No, wait.
That's one-in-five chance he'll die?

259
00:16:05.387 --> 00:16:07.379
I really wouldn't advise waiting.

260
00:16:07.457 --> 00:16:12.625
- Naomi, you gotta
start this treatment right away.
- What happens if I wait?

261
00:16:12.699 --> 00:16:18.368
Well, 29 weeks,
the survival rate is closer to 90%.

262
00:16:20.746 --> 00:16:24.013
I'm not doing the radiation.
But you'll die if-

263
00:16:24.085 --> 00:16:26.281
Listen. You know the chances.
They're nothing.

264
00:16:26.356 --> 00:16:28.518
But a few more weeks
will save the baby.

265
00:16:28.593 --> 00:16:33.329
Listen. You're depressed right now,
and you're not thinking right, so-

266
00:16:33.401 --> 00:16:36.269
Could you j-
Tell her, please.

267
00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:40.642
This cancer moves quick.
The median survival's two to four months.

268
00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:46.552
If you postpone- even for a week-

269
00:16:51.265 --> 00:16:53.700
I'm sorry, honey.

270
00:16:59.646 --> 00:17:03.675
As most of you know, Gregory House
recently gave a speech about me.
[Door Opens]

271
00:17:03.753 --> 00:17:05.779
I'd like to return the favor.

272
00:17:05.856 --> 00:17:08.155
- Sorry.
- Dr. Wilson.

273
00:17:09.161 --> 00:17:11.426
I was hoping you were
gonna miss this one.

274
00:17:13.803 --> 00:17:18.834
A man is the sum ofhis actions.
Here are a few of Dr. House's.

275
00:17:19.913 --> 00:17:24.181
He violated a D.N.R.
And was charged with assault.

276
00:17:24.254 --> 00:17:29.194
He brought a termite into the O.R.
And spat on a surgeon.

277
00:17:29.262 --> 00:17:33.462
He accepted a Corvette from a patient
who was a known member
of the New Jersey Mafia.

278
00:17:33.536 --> 00:17:35.300
- Ed, look-
- Edward.

279
00:17:35.372 --> 00:17:39.367
Edward. You look at anyone's career,
you can find things that are-

280
00:17:39.446 --> 00:17:41.142
These are the last three months.

281
00:17:41.215 --> 00:17:46.781
He's personally had
more complaints filed against him
than any department in this hospital.

282
00:17:46.858 --> 00:17:50.523
Okay. He's screwed-up.
He's miserable.

283
00:17:50.598 --> 00:17:55.368
And he should probably reread
the ethics code, but it works for him.
He's saved hundreds of lives.

284
00:17:55.439 --> 00:17:58.808
He is a drug addict
who flaunts his addiction
and refuses to get treatment.

285
00:17:58.879 --> 00:18:02.373
He is a disgrace
and an embarrassment
to this hospital.

286
00:18:03.587 --> 00:18:06.786
I'd go on,
but it gets kind of mean, so-

287
00:18:06.859 --> 00:18:08.828
I'm gonna keep this simple.

288
00:18:08.896 --> 00:18:10.831
House goes or I go.

289
00:18:10.899 --> 00:18:16.534
- You shouldn't personalize this.
- And by "I," I mean
my hundred million dollars.

290
00:18:20.081 --> 00:18:21.572
How's that for personalizing?

291
00:18:24.755 --> 00:18:26.690
You gave us that money
for a reason.

292
00:18:26.759 --> 00:18:29.558
Are you really willing
to throw it all away
because of one doctor?

293
00:18:29.631 --> 00:18:34.901
Gregory House is a symbol
of everything wrong
with the health care industry.

294
00:18:34.973 --> 00:18:37.876
Waste. Insubordination.

295
00:18:37.945 --> 00:18:42.647
Doctors preening like
they're kings, and the hospital is
their own private fiefdom.

296
00:18:42.719 --> 00:18:46.452
Health care is a business.
I'm gonna run it like one.

297
00:18:48.296 --> 00:18:51.027
I hereby move to revoke
the tenure of Dr. Gregory House...

298
00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:53.831
and terminate his employment
at this hospital, effective immediately.

299
00:18:53.905 --> 00:18:56.466
- Don't you think we should discuss this?
- We just did.

300
00:18:56.542 --> 00:18:58.943
- We need time-
- The vote is on the table.
All in favor?

301
00:19:31.769 --> 00:19:35.332
[Vogler]
Dr. Wilson.
Opposed.

302
00:19:35.408 --> 00:19:37.673
The motion is defeated.

303
00:19:39.615 --> 00:19:41.914
Dr. Wilson, would you mind
leaving the room, please?

304
00:19:41.986 --> 00:19:44.683
- Excuse me?
- We're going to take another vote.

305
00:19:45.893 --> 00:19:49.922
Well, first of all,
you can't void my vote
by making me stand in the hallway.

306
00:19:49.999 --> 00:19:52.730
And second,
you should check the bylaws.

307
00:19:52.804 --> 00:19:56.242
You need notice
and at least one business day
before you can reconsider any matter.

308
00:19:56.311 --> 00:20:00.010
We're voting on a different matter,
which you are conflicted out of.

309
00:20:00.083 --> 00:20:02.245
How can I be conflicted?

310
00:20:02.321 --> 00:20:05.120
This vote is whether
to dismiss Dr. James Wilson.

311
00:20:31.336 --> 00:20:33.328
[Machine Beeping]

312
00:20:39.817 --> 00:20:43.277
Naomi is refusing
to have the C-section.

313
00:20:43.356 --> 00:20:45.757
Her odds aren't good enough.

314
00:20:45.827 --> 00:20:49.697
They do suck.
Where's Wilson?

315
00:20:49.768 --> 00:20:52.602
Paged him twice.
She does this,
she knows she's gonna die.

316
00:20:52.673 --> 00:20:57.670
She's saving her child.
Cameron would point out
that people are capable of sacrifice.

317
00:20:57.747 --> 00:20:59.943
Cameron isn't here.

318
00:21:00.018 --> 00:21:03.786
- Perhaps proving her point.
- You think this woman
is making a rational decision?

319
00:21:03.857 --> 00:21:06.725
I think people can overcome
their baser drives.

320
00:21:06.796 --> 00:21:09.163
Pretty damn rarely.

321
00:21:09.233 --> 00:21:11.998
And not this time.
This is purely biological.

322
00:21:12.072 --> 00:21:15.669
In evolutionary terms,
the needs of the next generation
are more important.

323
00:21:15.745 --> 00:21:19.205
- You're saying she's making the right call?
- Darwin is. I'm not.

324
00:21:19.284 --> 00:21:21.879
The next generation is not my patient.

325
00:21:22.957 --> 00:21:25.654
We have to raise the odds
for Mommy.

326
00:21:25.728 --> 00:21:27.856
Where the hell is Wilson?
He's the oncologist.

327
00:21:27.932 --> 00:21:31.267
Good plan. Cure cancer.

328
00:21:31.337 --> 00:21:33.568
I'm surprised no one ever
thought of that before.

329
00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:36.972
There he is.

330
00:21:37.047 --> 00:21:39.482
Dr. House.

331
00:21:39.551 --> 00:21:43.148
You guys bust out?
We made bail. They won't let us
in our baby's room.

332
00:21:43.225 --> 00:21:47.288
Weird. You think they'd let you
take her home while they figured out
if you tried to kill her.

333
00:21:47.364 --> 00:21:49.731
We're good parents.
We fed her whenever she was hungry.

334
00:21:49.802 --> 00:21:52.033
Big meals. We had no idea
that diet was so bad.

335
00:21:52.106 --> 00:21:54.371
The nutritionist said
it had everything she needed.
Listen.

336
00:21:54.443 --> 00:21:58.940
The kid who stacks the free-range
grapefruit in your health food store
is not a nutritionist.

337
00:21:59.017 --> 00:22:00.952
But my uncle is.

338
00:22:01.021 --> 00:22:03.456
He went to college and everything.

339
00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:15.473
- Foreman, I need a C.T. Scan on-
- Olive Kaplan.

340
00:22:15.546 --> 00:22:17.242
Seriously?

341
00:22:19.820 --> 00:22:21.755
Olive Kaplan.

342
00:22:21.823 --> 00:22:25.192
Look for abscesses
or occult infections. Yeah.

343
00:22:25.262 --> 00:22:27.288
Bye-bye.

344
00:22:35.613 --> 00:22:38.276
Listen. Vogler's all about
clinical trials.

345
00:22:38.351 --> 00:22:40.320
The hospital's chock full of them.

346
00:22:40.387 --> 00:22:42.856
There's gotta be something
for small-cell lung cancer.

347
00:22:43.726 --> 00:22:45.661
What are you doing?

348
00:22:45.730 --> 00:22:48.029
I got sacked.

349
00:22:49.603 --> 00:22:51.629
Did you make a pass at Cuddy?

350
00:22:51.707 --> 00:22:54.176
I told you.
She only has thighs for me.

351
00:22:54.245 --> 00:22:56.146
I voted to keep you.

352
00:22:56.915 --> 00:23:00.580
So he's getting rid of
every board member
who votes to keep me around.

353
00:23:00.655 --> 00:23:03.181
[Chuckles]
Yeah. Every one of us.

354
00:23:03.260 --> 00:23:05.889
Just you?
Yep.

355
00:23:06.932 --> 00:23:09.265
But you're only off the board, right?

356
00:23:09.336 --> 00:23:12.671
They couldn't have gotten
unanimous approval for you.

357
00:23:12.742 --> 00:23:16.043
Brown from oncology voted no.
So did Cuddy,

358
00:23:16.115 --> 00:23:19.052
Taylor and Peavey.

359
00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:21.988
Oh, so you're off the board.
Big deal.

360
00:23:22.058 --> 00:23:24.118
Frees up Wednesday nights for bowling.

361
00:23:24.194 --> 00:23:26.925
You're still a doctor.
Getting dumped
looks great in Who's Who.

362
00:23:26.999 --> 00:23:29.093
Vogler gave me
the option of resigning.

363
00:23:29.938 --> 00:23:31.429
And I took it.

364
00:23:31.507 --> 00:23:34.410
Big of him.
I got no kids.

365
00:23:34.478 --> 00:23:37.243
My marriages sucks.
I only had two things
that worked for me.

366
00:23:37.317 --> 00:23:39.411
This job and this stupid
screwed-up friendship,

367
00:23:39.487 --> 00:23:41.922
and neither mattered enough to you
to give one lousy speech.

368
00:23:48.803 --> 00:23:50.795
They matter.

369
00:23:54.479 --> 00:23:57.780
If I could do it all again-
You'd do the same thing.

370
00:24:05.698 --> 00:24:09.136
Well, you'll be gone soon too.

371
00:24:16.583 --> 00:24:19.212
Those clinical trials?

372
00:24:26.700 --> 00:24:28.692
I'll make some calls.

373
00:24:31.575 --> 00:24:34.374
Thanks.

374
00:24:41.959 --> 00:24:45.226
It's- It's not cancer.
It's not gonna kill me?

375
00:24:45.298 --> 00:24:49.566
- It's hemorrhoids.
- But all that blood-
I mean, that can't be right.

376
00:24:49.639 --> 00:24:51.904
Looks worse than it is.

377
00:24:53.612 --> 00:24:55.672
- Nice job of protecting me.
- Can this wait?

378
00:24:55.749 --> 00:24:58.344
His ass can wait.
You save my job
by sacking Wilson?

379
00:24:58.420 --> 00:25:00.912
What did you think would happen
when you made that speech?

380
00:25:00.991 --> 00:25:04.429
That you would just pout
for a little while
and we'd all forgive you?

381
00:25:04.498 --> 00:25:07.263
You don't spit on the man
that signs your paycheck.

382
00:25:07.335 --> 00:25:09.896
First Cameron, then Wilson.

383
00:25:09.973 --> 00:25:11.703
You're next.
Pull your pants up.

384
00:25:11.777 --> 00:25:14.372
[House]
So it's about the money.
Of course it's about the money.

385
00:25:14.447 --> 00:25:19.547
The money Vogler gave,
he could have bought a few jets,
maybe a baseball team.

386
00:25:19.623 --> 00:25:22.753
Orjust stuck it in Chase Manhattan
and collected interest.

387
00:25:22.828 --> 00:25:27.291
But he gave it to us
to buy equipment, to do research.

388
00:25:27.369 --> 00:25:31.832
You are a great doctor, House,
but you are not worth
a hundred million dollars.

389
00:25:36.151 --> 00:25:38.313
[House]
We've sequenced the D.N.A.
Of the tumor cells.

390
00:25:38.388 --> 00:25:42.258
P53 gene mutation at codon 55.
She's perfect for your trial.

391
00:25:42.328 --> 00:25:44.797
Hmm. She's pretty far advanced.

392
00:25:45.867 --> 00:25:49.168
Well, you want easy cases,
you picked the wrong specialty.

393
00:25:52.746 --> 00:25:55.113
Otherwise in good health?
Excellent.

394
00:25:55.184 --> 00:25:58.644
When can she start?
Middle of next week.

395
00:25:58.722 --> 00:26:02.524
Cancer's already stage III.
It'd be a waste of time.
She can start in two days.

396
00:26:02.596 --> 00:26:05.191
She can't start in two days.
She's pregnant.

397
00:26:05.266 --> 00:26:07.792
She won't be in two days.

398
00:26:07.871 --> 00:26:10.967
- I've scheduled a C-section.
- She'd still have to wait a month.

399
00:26:11.043 --> 00:26:14.344
You can't take part in any trial
for at least 30 days
after major surgery.

400
00:26:14.416 --> 00:26:17.819
Well, it's definitely surgery, but major?

401
00:26:17.888 --> 00:26:22.224
It's not your call.
Again, question
of interpretation.

402
00:26:22.295 --> 00:26:24.321
You're scamming a doctor? Now?

403
00:26:24.399 --> 00:26:26.868
Come on. Vogler's looking for
any excuse to can you.

404
00:26:26.936 --> 00:26:29.371
Oh, I think he's got
a big bag of those already.

405
00:26:29.441 --> 00:26:33.174
These regulations aren't just
here to annoy you. Doing this
is dangerous to the patient.

406
00:26:33.248 --> 00:26:36.151
Well, I'll be sure
and let her know that.

407
00:26:36.219 --> 00:26:38.211
Care to join me?

408
00:26:40.627 --> 00:26:45.897
Angiogenesis inhibitors
prevent the tumors
from creating blood vessels.

409
00:26:45.969 --> 00:26:47.938
Without blood, the tumor starves.

410
00:26:48.006 --> 00:26:50.100
That sounds great.
What about the baby?

411
00:26:50.175 --> 00:26:53.908
The treatment would be fatal
to the baby.

412
00:26:53.982 --> 00:26:57.647
I've scheduled a C-section
for this afternoon.
No.

413
00:26:57.722 --> 00:27:00.750
It's in the trial phase right now,
but so far...

414
00:27:00.827 --> 00:27:03.923
complete remission in
more than 30% of subjects.

415
00:27:03.999 --> 00:27:08.769
- I told Dr. Foreman I didn't want a C-section.
- When your chances of living were less
than a third of what they are now.

416
00:27:10.644 --> 00:27:12.636
Well, if the baby's
premature, then-

417
00:27:12.714 --> 00:27:16.083
Our Pediatrics department has
the best neonatal I.C.U. In the state.

418
00:27:16.153 --> 00:27:19.124
No. His lungs. His brain.
He's not ready.

419
00:27:19.192 --> 00:27:22.357
And he could be fine.
You don't know what it's like
raising a sick child.

420
00:27:22.431 --> 00:27:26.426
[Sean]
His odds are much better
than yours are.

421
00:27:26.504 --> 00:27:29.873
You have to let them at least try this.

422
00:27:29.943 --> 00:27:32.276
- Talk to her.
- Okay.

423
00:27:33.282 --> 00:27:35.274
Leave the room.

424
00:27:36.387 --> 00:27:38.322
Okay.

425
00:27:47.606 --> 00:27:50.600
How long have you
been taking oxybutynin?

426
00:27:50.678 --> 00:27:52.670
Uh, since I was about 20.

427
00:27:54.017 --> 00:27:57.250
Incontinence is pretty uncommon
in a woman of your age.

428
00:27:57.323 --> 00:27:59.849
It's even more bizarre
in a woman in her 20s.

429
00:27:59.927 --> 00:28:02.864
I guess I haven't had the best luck
when it comes to my health.

430
00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:06.526
Seems that way.

431
00:28:06.605 --> 00:28:11.170
You said to your husband,
"You don't know what it's like
raising a sick child."

432
00:28:11.246 --> 00:28:14.045
You didn't say, " You don't know
what it would be like."

433
00:28:17.190 --> 00:28:19.216
This is not your first child, is it?

434
00:28:21.396 --> 00:28:23.388
And he doesn't know.

435
00:28:27.808 --> 00:28:29.800
I was 18.

436
00:28:29.877 --> 00:28:32.973
I got pregnant, got married.

437
00:28:33.050 --> 00:28:37.581
I had the most beautiful
little girl. Grace.

438
00:28:39.861 --> 00:28:42.456
She had infantile Alexander's disease.

439
00:28:44.402 --> 00:28:47.840
I'm sorry.
Two years
we watched her die.

440
00:28:47.908 --> 00:28:51.243
My husband was a-
Uh, my first husband was a-

441
00:28:52.616 --> 00:28:55.313
a great guy,

442
00:28:55.387 --> 00:28:59.291
but after that I couldn't even
look at him without thinking of her.

443
00:28:59.361 --> 00:29:02.092
I left him.

444
00:29:02.166 --> 00:29:05.433
I left my job.
I left everything.
Very moving story.

445
00:29:05.505 --> 00:29:08.806
Explains why you're being so selfish.

446
00:29:08.877 --> 00:29:10.971
I'm willing to die
to protect my husband.

447
00:29:11.047 --> 00:29:14.541
Because it's what you want.
Your husband wants you to live.

448
00:29:14.620 --> 00:29:18.615
Well, he doesn't understand-
Oh, who the hell does?

449
00:29:18.693 --> 00:29:20.662
Tragedies happen.

450
00:29:20.730 --> 00:29:23.997
If you think that turning
yourself into a disposable
incubator for a few weeks...

451
00:29:24.069 --> 00:29:27.336
is gonna protect your baby
from all the crap in this world,
go ahead.

452
00:29:27.408 --> 00:29:30.573
Die happy.
I got no problem
with people killing themselves.

453
00:29:30.647 --> 00:29:32.639
But don't think it makes you a hero.

454
00:29:45.104 --> 00:29:47.096
Okay.

455
00:29:50.147 --> 00:29:53.015
You're scheduled for 4:00 p.m.

456
00:30:00.030 --> 00:30:02.090
Yes. This is Dr. Lim.

457
00:30:04.304 --> 00:30:06.296
[Woman Speaks, Indistinct]

458
00:30:09.312 --> 00:30:11.645
Count down from 10.

459
00:30:11.717 --> 00:30:14.312
Okay.

460
00:30:14.387 --> 00:30:16.413
Ten,

461
00:30:16.491 --> 00:30:18.824
nine,

462
00:30:18.895 --> 00:30:20.887
eight-

463
00:30:22.434 --> 00:30:25.428
[Man] Tray setup.
That seemed kind of fast.
Is she all right?

464
00:30:25.506 --> 00:30:27.407
She's fine.

465
00:30:30.582 --> 00:30:34.145
Wake her up.
That was Vogler. Surgery is off.

466
00:30:40.699 --> 00:30:42.827
[Elevator Bell Dings]

467
00:30:44.038 --> 00:30:47.168
Hey! You're killing her!

468
00:30:47.243 --> 00:30:51.706
Really? I thought you were the one
trying to ram her into a drug trial
five minutes after surgery.

469
00:30:51.784 --> 00:30:53.810
She knows the risk.
She was fully informed.

470
00:30:53.888 --> 00:30:57.018
Well, the guy running
the study sure wasn't.
Not his life. Not his call.

471
00:30:57.093 --> 00:31:00.121
- His study, his call.
- Right. So she kicks off,
his numbers look bad.

472
00:31:00.198 --> 00:31:02.497
The numbers look bad,
the study looks bad.

473
00:31:02.569 --> 00:31:05.665
Which would cost you money!
And keep a lifesaving
protocol off the market.

474
00:31:05.741 --> 00:31:08.472
One person! One blip in the data!

475
00:31:08.546 --> 00:31:10.879
Ever heard of the F.D.A.?
They eat blips for breakfast.

476
00:31:10.950 --> 00:31:12.919
One person should never
endanger thousands.

477
00:31:12.986 --> 00:31:16.287
Well, thank God you were here
to save all those lives!

478
00:31:17.794 --> 00:31:19.786
[Chuckles]

479
00:31:23.370 --> 00:31:25.396
The board's meeting again
this evening.

480
00:31:25.475 --> 00:31:28.571
Why don't you settle down,
play some Game Boy?

481
00:31:28.646 --> 00:31:30.808
Why don't you watch your soap?

482
00:31:30.883 --> 00:31:35.083
I hear they're firing
the handsome doctor today.
Boy, that should be a good one.

483
00:31:47.545 --> 00:31:49.673
If we had the C-section anyway,

484
00:31:49.748 --> 00:31:52.776
she could still do
the experimental treatment, right?

485
00:31:52.853 --> 00:31:57.486
- We'd just have to wait 30 days.
- Assuming the doctor running the trial
isn't too pissed off to let her in.

486
00:31:57.562 --> 00:32:00.727
And assuming I'm even
healthy enough to-

487
00:32:00.801 --> 00:32:02.827
- Honey.
- [Machine Beeping]

488
00:32:02.904 --> 00:32:06.467
- Are you okay?
- [Chase] Sats are dropping-
down to the 80s. Stay with us, Naomi.

489
00:32:06.544 --> 00:32:09.309
What's going on?
[Chase]
We need you to leave the room.

490
00:32:10.684 --> 00:32:12.619
Respiratory distress.

491
00:32:12.687 --> 00:32:15.282
- Could you tell me
what's going on?
- We're trying to find out.

492
00:32:15.358 --> 00:32:17.327
[Machines Beeping]

493
00:32:18.697 --> 00:32:21.258
[Woman]
Here.
Still kicking.

494
00:32:21.335 --> 00:32:23.361
Flash pulmonary edema?

495
00:32:23.439 --> 00:32:26.000
Lungs are clear.
Here it is.

496
00:32:26.076 --> 00:32:28.170
- Pulmonary embolus.
- Gotta get her to an O.R.

497
00:32:28.247 --> 00:32:30.773
[Woman]
Now. Right away.
[Sean] Uh, what happened?

498
00:32:30.852 --> 00:32:34.017
It's an embolism- a blood clot.
Fairly common with lung cancer.

499
00:32:34.090 --> 00:32:38.553
It's not a full saddle embolism. So blood's
still trickling through. We've been able
to get Naomi breathing a little,

500
00:32:38.631 --> 00:32:42.262
but we need to remove the clot,
and we need you to approve the treatment.
Of course.

501
00:32:42.338 --> 00:32:45.309
Whatever you have to do, just do it.
It's not that simple.

502
00:32:45.376 --> 00:32:48.814
The best course for the baby
would be an immediate C-section.
The longer we postpone,

503
00:32:48.882 --> 00:32:52.650
the greater chance he'll have
brain damage from lack of oxygen.
Fine. Just do it.

504
00:32:52.722 --> 00:32:54.691
Here's the problem.

505
00:32:54.758 --> 00:32:59.357
The C-section would be
very, very dangerous for Naomi.
Dangerous like-

506
00:33:00.968 --> 00:33:04.269
In her current condition,
there's a real chance she won't survive.

507
00:33:05.911 --> 00:33:07.846
I'm sorry.

508
00:33:07.914 --> 00:33:11.113
Your wife's unconscious.
We need you to make a decision.

509
00:33:15.426 --> 00:33:18.989
I just want her to live.

510
00:33:19.066 --> 00:33:21.058
No C-section.

511
00:33:33.991 --> 00:33:36.688
Sats are still way down.
We gotta push the streptokinase.

512
00:33:36.762 --> 00:33:39.357
Too risky. Even if it dissolves the clot,
she could still bleed out-

513
00:33:39.434 --> 00:33:42.530
- She's hemodynamically compromised.
- It's not good for the baby.

514
00:33:42.605 --> 00:33:44.096
Dad doesn't care.

515
00:33:47.881 --> 00:33:50.544
Bolusing 250,000 units.

516
00:33:50.619 --> 00:33:53.418
[Machine Beeping Rapidly]
B.P.'s dropping.

517
00:33:53.491 --> 00:33:55.858
Pressors.
Don't have time.
We've gotta suck it out.

518
00:33:55.928 --> 00:33:57.760
[Beeping Continues]

519
00:33:57.832 --> 00:33:59.698
Systolic B.P.'s 80.

520
00:34:03.842 --> 00:34:05.834
B.P.'s stabilizing.

521
00:34:05.911 --> 00:34:09.246
O2 sats rising.

522
00:34:12.223 --> 00:34:14.385
- Did you get the clot?
- I think so.

523
00:34:14.459 --> 00:34:18.090
She's stabilized.
How long was her oxygen at that level?

524
00:34:18.166 --> 00:34:21.433
- About 10 minutes.
- Brain function compromised?

525
00:34:21.505 --> 00:34:24.066
Shouldn't be, but we'll-
[Beeping]

526
00:34:24.143 --> 00:34:27.478
B.P.'s dropping.
Up the dopamine.

527
00:34:27.548 --> 00:34:29.779
- She's not responding. How much?
- Up to 30 micrograms.

528
00:34:29.852 --> 00:34:32.789
[Chase]
Is she septic?

529
00:34:32.857 --> 00:34:35.622
She's bleeding into her abdomen.

530
00:34:35.695 --> 00:34:37.687
We won't be able to stop it.

531
00:34:39.936 --> 00:34:42.497
[Sighs]
I'll go talk to the husband.

532
00:34:42.574 --> 00:34:47.344
No. You stay here.
Keep her as stable as you can
for as long as you can.

533
00:34:56.163 --> 00:34:59.498
She had trauma
during the procedure.

534
00:35:00.904 --> 00:35:03.339
She's bleeding into her abdomen.

535
00:35:04.411 --> 00:35:06.346
There's nothing we can do.
I'm sorry.

536
00:35:06.414 --> 00:35:09.681
Oh. No.

537
00:35:09.752 --> 00:35:12.814
I need you to okay the C-section.
That's gonna kill her, right?

538
00:35:12.892 --> 00:35:15.327
Probably will.

539
00:35:15.395 --> 00:35:18.332
I can't do that.

540
00:35:18.400 --> 00:35:20.562
She's dying either way.

541
00:35:20.638 --> 00:35:24.337
- I'm- I'm sorry.
- Stay with me, Sean.
I need your okay on this.

542
00:35:26.781 --> 00:35:28.750
She makes the decisions, and I'm-

543
00:35:28.819 --> 00:35:31.881
Right. And that's gonna be
tough from now on,
but this decision is easy.

544
00:35:33.760 --> 00:35:35.854
You know what she'd want.
Yeah.

545
00:35:37.400 --> 00:35:40.701
I can't do-
You make this call,
only two things change.

546
00:35:40.772 --> 00:35:45.576
One, yeah, you feel guilty
for killing your wife.
Two, your baby lives.

547
00:35:47.684 --> 00:35:49.983
Naomi's baby lives.

548
00:35:55.964 --> 00:35:57.933
Okay. Okay.

549
00:36:08.152 --> 00:36:10.314
[Man]
He's out.
Umbilical cord's clamped.

550
00:36:10.388 --> 00:36:13.848
- [Chase]
No respiration.
- [Foreman] His lungs aren't opening up.

551
00:36:13.928 --> 00:36:15.863
They aren't mature.

552
00:36:15.931 --> 00:36:18.959
[Foreman]
Come on. Take a breath.
You know you can do it.

553
00:36:19.036 --> 00:36:22.371
- [Beeping]
- What you got?

554
00:36:22.443 --> 00:36:24.605
Looks like V-fib.
[Foreman]
Pulse?

555
00:36:24.679 --> 00:36:27.707
- No. Paddles.
- [Woman]
Right here.

556
00:36:27.784 --> 00:36:30.549
Come on. Come on.

557
00:36:31.591 --> 00:36:33.856
- Clear.!
- [Beeping]

558
00:36:33.929 --> 00:36:35.989
- Nothing.
- Charging.

559
00:36:36.065 --> 00:36:38.125
- Good boy. Open up.
- How's he doin'?

560
00:36:39.070 --> 00:36:41.005
Still not breathing.
We've gotta intubate.

561
00:36:41.073 --> 00:36:43.304
Clear!

562
00:36:43.378 --> 00:36:44.869
[Beeping]

563
00:36:45.982 --> 00:36:47.917
[Baby Cries]

564
00:36:58.469 --> 00:37:00.961
[Crying]

565
00:37:20.240 --> 00:37:22.368
Thank you.

566
00:37:22.444 --> 00:37:24.640
I'm late for the board meeting.
We need to talk.

567
00:37:24.715 --> 00:37:26.775
I don't want to hear it.
It's about a patient.

568
00:37:26.851 --> 00:37:30.380
The pregnant woman?
She wasn't qualified for that trial.
And I'm not gonna apologize-

569
00:37:30.458 --> 00:37:35.228
I'm not talking about her. At this point,
I think it's best if I concentrate
on patients who are still alive.

570
00:37:37.168 --> 00:37:41.004
Pulmonary embolism.
She bled out. Saved her son.

571
00:37:42.811 --> 00:37:47.478
This is Olive Kaplan's C.T. Scan-
the incredible shrinking baby.

572
00:37:51.993 --> 00:37:53.985
Her thymus gland.

573
00:37:54.064 --> 00:37:58.025
DiGeorge syndrome.
It's genetic. Caused the gland
to wither to nothing.

574
00:37:58.104 --> 00:38:00.699
This is why she couldn't gain weight.
Yeah.

575
00:38:01.843 --> 00:38:05.713
I'll call the police and Social Services
and have all the charges withdrawn.

576
00:38:05.784 --> 00:38:10.281
I've sent a test down to confirm.
When it comes back, you should start Olive
on immunoglobulin replacement.

577
00:38:10.358 --> 00:38:12.884
You're not gonna do it?

578
00:38:14.398 --> 00:38:16.663
Well, I assume I won't be here.

579
00:38:20.909 --> 00:38:22.901
[Sighs]

580
00:38:39.340 --> 00:38:41.707
Your boy is doing good.

581
00:39:01.612 --> 00:39:06.609
[Vogler]
It's the same motion
as yesterday, people. Same reasons.

582
00:39:07.688 --> 00:39:11.126
All those in favor of dismissing
Gregory House, raise a hand.

583
00:39:17.371 --> 00:39:19.772
[Sighs]
Dr. Cuddy,

584
00:39:19.842 --> 00:39:23.439
you realize
this is going to happen.

585
00:39:27.689 --> 00:39:30.181
- I can't do it.
- You can't abstain.

586
00:39:32.363 --> 00:39:34.332
I'm not abstaining.
I'm voting no.

587
00:39:36.102 --> 00:39:38.071
You've changed your mind
since yesterday?

588
00:39:38.140 --> 00:39:41.600
What did he do?
Buy you dinner and roses?
Threaten to drown your dog?

589
00:39:41.679 --> 00:39:44.012
- He did his job.
- Right.

590
00:39:44.083 --> 00:39:46.018
He saved another life.

591
00:39:46.086 --> 00:39:47.782
Maybe.
Good for him.

592
00:39:47.855 --> 00:39:50.222
- It's great. It's not the point.
- It's what we do.

593
00:39:50.293 --> 00:39:53.958
And you could do it
a lot better if you didn't
have to worry about some madman...

594
00:39:54.033 --> 00:39:56.059
running around the hospital
accountable to no one.

595
00:39:56.136 --> 00:39:59.039
- But that's not the choice
you're giving us.
- House won't listen to anyone.

596
00:39:59.108 --> 00:40:03.171
And you're not accountable
to anybody either.
Because you think you own us.

597
00:40:03.248 --> 00:40:06.583
I move for the immediate dismissal
of Dr. Lisa Cuddy.

598
00:40:06.654 --> 00:40:08.486
[Simpson]
She's upset. We all are.

599
00:40:08.558 --> 00:40:10.891
Why would you risk
your career to save him?

600
00:40:15.235 --> 00:40:18.832
If you think House deserves to go-
If you think I deserve to go,

601
00:40:18.908 --> 00:40:22.607
Wilson deserved to go,
then vote yes.

602
00:40:22.681 --> 00:40:27.553
But if you're doing this because
you are afraid of losing
his money, then he's right.

603
00:40:27.623 --> 00:40:29.615
He does own you.

604
00:40:36.872 --> 00:40:40.776
You have a choice.
Maybe the last real one
you'll have here.

605
00:40:43.917 --> 00:40:45.909
[Door Opens]

606
00:40:47.857 --> 00:40:49.849
[Door Closes]

607
00:40:53.167 --> 00:40:56.661
- [All Laughing]
- Cuddy is a genius.

608
00:40:56.739 --> 00:41:00.609
Convincing four people to give up
a fortune to save our sorry asses.

609
00:41:01.915 --> 00:41:05.080
- [House]
Dr. Cuddy, the man of the hour.
- [All] Hey, hey!

610
00:41:05.153 --> 00:41:07.952
Hey.
What are you doing?

611
00:41:08.025 --> 00:41:11.190
We're drinking. I would have
thought that was pretty obvious.

612
00:41:11.263 --> 00:41:13.698
To the great champion.
Saved you,

613
00:41:13.768 --> 00:41:15.964
saved Wilson-
saved the whole team.

614
00:41:27.591 --> 00:41:32.293
Of course none of them would have
needed saving if you could actually
get along with another human being.

615
00:41:32.366 --> 00:41:35.360
Thank you, Miss Buzz Kill.

616
00:41:35.438 --> 00:41:38.203
Well, you only cost us
a hundred million dollars.

617
00:41:38.276 --> 00:41:40.370
Could have saved some lives,

618
00:41:40.446 --> 00:41:43.508
could have made a fewjobs,
helped a few people-yippee.

619
00:41:43.584 --> 00:41:45.712
You voted to get rid of him.

620
00:41:45.789 --> 00:41:47.781
The lesser of two evils.

621
00:41:50.263 --> 00:41:52.425
You should be mourning.

622
00:41:52.500 --> 00:41:54.492
I know I am.

623
00:44:03.254 --> 00:44:04.516
That's some bad hat, Harry.

9999
00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>

